{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778376347757,"sessionID":"ses_1f083c521ffebQaAU412bEAqlk","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_jOWVrbP3f4T9upoROznqLfTD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `CL_0001041` so the CXCR3 (`PR_000001207`) restriction uses `has plasma membrane part` (`RO_0002104`) instead of `has part`, matching the requested hierarchy revision.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+## Summary\n+\n+This change updates `CL_0001041` (`CD8-positive, CXCR3-positive, alpha-beta regulatory T cell`) so the CXCR3 (`PR_000001207`) logical restriction uses `has plasma membrane part` (`RO_0002104`) instead of `has part` (`BFO_0000051`). This better reflects CXCR3 membrane localization and aligns the class with related CXCR3-positive T cell patterns already using `RO_0002104`.\n+\n+I also added an `IAO_0000233` tracker annotation linking `CL_0001041` back to issue #3382, following the existing tracker annotation pattern in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- Reviewed the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Checked the existing `CL_0001041` axioms in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Compared related CXCR3 (`PR_000001207`) usages, including CXCR3-positive classes using `RO_0002104` and CXCR3-negative classes using the negative plasma membrane part relation.\n+- Made the minimal ontology edit requested by the issue.\n+- Ran `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-3382.owl` successfully to check syntax.\n+\n+Signed-off-by: GitHub Copilot\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval